you can take a chance on me.

247
00:20:30,113 --> 00:20:31,198
Excuse me?

248
00:20:32,282 --> 00:20:33,533
You must be her friend.

249
00:20:34,326 --> 00:20:36,036
- Take a seat. Come on now.
- Okay...

250
00:20:38,538 --> 00:20:40,874
Do you want me to show you
some magic tricks?

251
00:20:41,875 --> 00:20:42,876
Okay.

252
00:20:43,460 --> 00:20:44,753
Let me see this.

253
00:20:44,836 --> 00:20:45,837
No!

254
00:20:49,591 --> 00:20:51,760
This way

255
00:20:52,302 --> 00:20:53,470
it's half-Chan.

256
00:20:53,553 --> 00:20:54,554
No...

257
00:20:55,430 --> 00:20:56,848
Heart-Chan.

258
00:20:58,266 --> 00:20:59,267
Bother-Chan.

259
00:21:03,146 --> 00:21:04,856
The magic
of sticking it back together.

260
00:21:05,899 --> 00:21:07,359
The magic of tearing it apart.

261
00:21:07,526 --> 00:21:09,569
Together, apart, repeat.

262
00:21:09,653 --> 00:21:12,948
<i>Chant his name</i>

263
00:21:13,031 --> 00:21:16,702
<i>Goodbye, my love, Chan</i>

264
00:21:19,913 --> 00:21:20,914
Excuse me.

265
00:21:25,127 --> 00:21:26,336
Chan...

266
00:21:27,254 --> 00:21:28,505
No...

267
00:21:37,806 --> 00:21:38,932
That scared me.

268
00:21:40,100 --> 00:21:42,728
Today would've been a perfect day

269
00:21:43,687 --> 00:21:46,690
if I'd only managed
to have Chan's poster in one piece.

270
00:21:49,693 --> 00:21:50,694
Chan.

271
00:22:00,579 --> 00:22:02,497
It was going pretty well.

272
00:22:03,999 --> 00:22:06,585
What do girls like so much
about that guy, Lee Chan, anyway?

273
00:22:06,668 --> 00:22:08,462
He used to be nothing
but an outcast and a loser.

274
00:22:09,671 --> 00:22:11,590
<i>He used to be nothing
but an outcast and a loser.</i>

275
00:22:11,673 --> 00:22:15,927
<i>An outcast and a loser.</i>

276
00:22:17,971 --> 00:22:19,181
"Outcast"?

277
00:22:21,266 --> 00:22:22,684
"Loser"?

278
00:22:26,521 --> 00:22:28,899
There she goes again.
Let's go stop her.

279
00:22:35,405 --> 00:22:38,325
I bet
people can't even imagine his past.

280
00:22:48,543 --> 00:22:50,420
- Was it you?
- Excuse me?

281
00:22:50,504 --> 00:22:53,590
You were the one bullying
and isolating him

282
00:22:54,216 --> 00:22:55,217
weren't you?

283
00:22:55,759 --> 00:23:00,430
I'm never going to forgive you!

284
00:23:21,535 --> 00:23:22,661
Your nose is bleeding.

285
00:23:27,249 --> 00:23:28,667
We're sorry.

286
00:23:29,417 --> 00:23:30,585
We're so sorry.

287
00:23:31,336 --> 00:23:34,464
My friend has been having
such a hard time finding a job

288
00:23:34,881 --> 00:23:36,967
- and life has been so rough
- You did well.

289
00:23:37,050 --> 00:23:39,511
that she ended up developing
anger management issues.

290
00:23:39,594 --> 00:23:41,263
We're truly sorry.

291
00:23:41,346 --> 00:23:42,931
We're so, truly sorry.

292
00:23:43,181 --> 00:23:46,142
What are you apologizing for?
I'm not sorry at all.

293
00:23:47,018 --> 00:23:49,437
Bullying is the worst.

294
00:23:50,021 --> 00:23:52,190
Do you even know what that's like?

295
00:23:58,071 --> 00:23:59,322
I'm sorry.

296
00:24:00,365 --> 00:24:02,576
You don't, do you?

297
00:24:15,589 --> 00:24:16,631
- Jeez.
- What are they doing?

298
00:24:17,048 --> 00:24:18,133
- What the...
- Did he hit her?

299
00:24:30,812 --> 00:24:35,775
My friend is so deeply apologetic
that she's on her knees.

300
00:24:35,859 --> 00:24:37,694
I guess she's reflecting
on her actions a lot, right?

301
00:24:38,278 --> 00:24:39,404
Right?

302
00:24:41,531 --> 00:24:42,574
Well...

303
00:24:43,450 --> 00:24:44,701
That's enough. Just leave.

304
00:24:45,410 --> 00:24:47,120
How generous of you.

305
00:24:47,203 --> 00:24:48,997
Bless you. Thank you.

306
00:24:49,080 --> 00:24:50,498
Thank you.

307
00:24:51,333 --> 00:24:52,417
Bye.

308
00:24:52,500 --> 00:24:54,878
Right?

309
00:24:55,128 --> 00:24:57,589
- Hey, let go of me!
- Knock it off.

310
00:24:57,923 --> 00:24:58,965
What?

311
00:24:59,424 --> 00:25:01,551
She got anger management issues
because she couldn't get a job?

312
00:25:03,136 --> 00:25:04,471
For someone who works at SE.

313
00:25:04,846 --> 00:25:05,972
Do you know her?

314
00:25:08,266 --> 00:25:09,476
She's a stranger.

315
00:25:10,226 --> 00:25:11,227
Exactly.

316
00:25:12,020 --> 00:25:13,188
I should've asked for her number.

317
00:25:14,105 --> 00:25:15,148
Hurry up.

318
00:25:16,232 --> 00:25:17,317
Jeez, wait.

319
00:25:19,569 --> 00:25:20,737
- Throw her.
- Throw her.

320
00:25:25,367 --> 00:25:26,493
Oh, man.

321
00:25:26,910 --> 00:25:27,953
It's like

322
00:25:28,119 --> 00:25:30,372
her weight literally doubled
the second she got drunk.

323
00:25:30,455 --> 00:25:31,539
Darn it.

324
00:25:35,377 --> 00:25:36,836
This is nuts.

325
00:25:38,338 --> 00:25:40,006
FOREVER LEE CHAN

326
00:25:40,090 --> 00:25:43,093
Goodness. Anyway,
I guess Da-reum really is

327
00:25:43,426 --> 00:25:45,679
living out the ultimate
successful fan.

328
00:25:47,055 --> 00:25:48,431
I wonder if Chan even knows

329
00:25:49,015 --> 00:25:50,892
that he still has such a die-hard fan

330
00:25:50,976 --> 00:25:52,852
when D.N.X disbanded a decade ago.

331
00:25:54,020 --> 00:25:55,063
Beats me.

332
00:25:56,272 --> 00:25:58,441
Hey, let's go home.

333
00:26:00,652 --> 00:26:01,903
Oh, wait.

334
00:26:05,407 --> 00:26:06,533
Come on, let's go.

335
00:26:55,081 --> 00:26:57,208
SUNGJU STATION

336
00:27:02,922 --> 00:27:04,049
SUNGJU STATION

337
00:27:51,012 --> 00:27:53,515
Which department are you in?

338
00:27:53,598 --> 00:27:55,642
I'm with the Merchandising Team.

339
00:27:56,518 --> 00:27:58,186
I'm in Marketing.

340
00:27:58,269 --> 00:27:59,771
Marketing? Me too.

341
00:27:59,854 --> 00:28:02,107
- Really?
- I hope we get along.

342
00:28:02,190 --> 00:28:04,067
My name is Park Young-woo.

343
00:28:04,150 --> 00:28:05,235
What are your names?

344
00:28:05,318 --> 00:28:08,113
My name is Lee Min-a.

345
00:28:08,196 --> 00:28:09,280
- Lee Min-a.
- Lee Min-a.

346
00:28:09,364 --> 00:28:10,782
My name is Nam Da-reum.

347
00:28:10,865 --> 00:28:13,493
- Nam Da-reum. Lee Min-a and Da-reum.
- Nam Da-reum.

348
00:28:13,576 --> 00:28:14,828
I see.

349
00:28:16,079 --> 00:28:17,372
Let's get along.

350
00:28:17,664 --> 00:28:19,874
You know they say
loyalty to your batchmates is key.

351
00:28:19,958 --> 00:28:21,543
- How about a fist bump?
- Sure.

352
00:28:22,836 --> 00:28:24,379
You guys became close already?

353
00:28:27,215 --> 00:28:30,051
Congratulations
on joining the Appello family.

354
00:28:30,135 --> 00:28:31,803
I'm Kim Mi-young

355
00:28:32,053 --> 00:28:35,515
the Marketing Team Manager.
I'll be running today's orientation.

356
00:28:36,558 --> 00:28:38,601
Here are your employee ID cards.

357
00:28:39,894 --> 00:28:41,855
- Mr. Young-woo.
- Thank you.

358
00:28:41,938 --> 00:28:43,565
- Ms. Min-a.
- Thank you.

359
00:28:43,773 --> 00:28:45,150
And Ms. Da-reum.

360
00:28:47,735 --> 00:28:48,945
Thank you.

361
00:28:49,445 --> 00:28:52,115
<i>Appello currently has 82 employees</i>

362
00:28:52,198 --> 00:28:54,159
<i>plus three new hires joining today.</i>

363
00:28:54,242 --> 00:28:57,203
<i>That means this ID card is basically
Chan's limited-edition merch</i>

364
00:28:57,287 --> 00:28:59,998
<i>with only 85 of them
in the whole world.</i>

365
00:29:00,790 --> 00:29:03,459
<i>It's even customized!</i>

366
00:29:04,210 --> 00:29:07,630
All right, then. Let's dive
into the official company overview.

367
00:29:08,298 --> 00:29:09,465
- Shall we?
- Yes, ma'am.

368
00:29:09,549 --> 00:29:10,550
This way.

369
00:29:13,678 --> 00:29:15,430
- Come this way.
- Yes, ma'am.

370
00:29:22,979 --> 00:29:24,272
They come in different colors...

371
00:29:25,982 --> 00:29:27,233
Ms. Min-a.

372
00:29:29,235 --> 00:29:32,405
<i>Most of Appello's partner brands
are centered online</i>

373
00:29:32,488 --> 00:29:35,825
<i>we host pop-up spaces on floor one
so they can meet customers in person.</i>

374
00:29:35,909 --> 00:29:36,951
It's all right.

375
00:29:37,785 --> 00:29:40,121
<i>We also offer spaces for our brands</i>

376
00:29:40,205 --> 00:29:42,498
<i>such as sewing rooms,
pattern rooms, and studios.</i>

377
00:29:43,249 --> 00:29:46,252
<i>As you can see,
our dress code is completely free.</i>

378
00:29:46,336 --> 00:29:48,713
<i>From tomorrow on, you can wear
a swimsuit, party clothes</i>

379
00:29:48,796 --> 00:29:50,131
<i>or anything that fits your style.</i>

380
00:29:59,599 --> 00:30:02,352
<i>This is the studio
for lookbook and campaign shoots.</i>

381
00:30:02,977 --> 00:30:05,396
<i>All of Appello's visual content is
basically born right here.</i>

382
00:30:25,291 --> 00:30:26,334
NAM DA-REUM

383
00:30:26,834 --> 00:30:30,505
On the fourth floor, we have
Marketing and Merchandising Teams.

384
00:30:32,590 --> 00:30:34,467
Oh, and the CEO's Office.

385
00:30:38,179 --> 00:30:41,391
All right. For our final stop,
let's go meet the CEO.

386
00:30:41,474 --> 00:30:43,810
- What, right now?
- Yes.

387
00:30:58,992 --> 00:31:01,744
Hello, I'm the new hire, Nam Da-reum.

388
00:31:02,870 --> 00:31:03,913
Too cheesy.

389
00:31:07,208 --> 00:31:09,294
Nice to meet you. I'm Nam Da-reum.

390
00:31:09,377 --> 00:31:10,670
"I'm Nam Da-reum."

391
00:31:11,462 --> 00:31:12,672
You sound like a call center agent.

392
00:31:14,173 --> 00:31:15,508
Just act normal.

393
00:31:15,758 --> 00:31:17,135
And don't freeze up in front of Chan.

394
00:31:19,053 --> 00:31:20,638
Here, a secret weapon.

395
00:31:25,143 --> 00:31:27,312
Take this calming pill,
and it will help with your nerves.

396
00:31:28,646 --> 00:31:29,897
The calming pill.

397
00:31:37,947 --> 00:31:38,948
{\an8}Don't worry about the details.

398
00:31:40,575 --> 00:31:42,827
{\an8}I will send you the final proposal
by tomorrow morning.

399
00:31:44,203 --> 00:31:45,204
{\an8}Thank you.

400
00:31:45,913 --> 00:31:46,914
Mr. Kang.

401
00:31:48,541 --> 00:31:50,418
They are our new recruits.

402
00:31:56,799 --> 00:31:59,427
- It's nice to meet you.
- I'm new! I mean I'm Park Young-woo.

403
00:32:01,429 --> 00:32:02,472
It's nice to meet you.

404
00:32:02,555 --> 00:32:06,309
Hello, I'm the new hire, Lee Min-a.

405
00:32:16,194 --> 00:32:17,320
It's nice to meet you.

406
00:32:35,588 --> 00:32:38,299
<i>Is that you, Chan?</i>

407
00:32:45,890 --> 00:32:48,893
<i>What the? Why is it someone else?</i>

408
00:32:53,314 --> 00:32:54,732
I'm Nam Da-reum.

409
00:32:55,900 --> 00:32:57,193
NAM DA-REUM

410
00:33:01,489 --> 00:33:03,491
Welcome to Appello.

411
00:33:03,574 --> 00:33:06,411
My door is always open,
so feel free to drop by anytime.

412
00:33:07,078 --> 00:33:09,664
Don't feel too intimidated,
and just treat me as a coworker.

413
00:33:10,581 --> 00:33:12,417
Let's do some great work together.

414
00:33:12,959 --> 00:33:14,001
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir.

415
00:33:14,752 --> 00:33:17,130
All right. Shall we wrap up here
and head out?

416
00:33:17,463 --> 00:33:19,465
- Thank you.
- Goodbye.

417
00:33:26,431 --> 00:33:27,640
<i>It's Chan.</i>

418
00:33:43,489 --> 00:33:44,615
Ms. Nam.

419
00:33:50,455 --> 00:33:51,831
Ms. Da-reum? What's wrong?

420
00:33:51,914 --> 00:33:54,584
- Are you okay? Try to breathe.
- Ms. Da-reum.

421
00:33:54,792 --> 00:33:56,252
- Please call 911.
- Breathe.

422
00:33:56,335 --> 00:33:58,004
- What is it?
- Is something stuck in her throat?

423
00:33:58,087 --> 00:33:59,797
- You can't breathe?
- What's wrong?

424
00:33:59,881 --> 00:34:00,923
- Goodness.
- Breathe.

425
00:34:01,048 --> 00:34:02,508
Try to breathe.

426
00:34:36,626 --> 00:34:37,668
Da-reum...

427
00:34:38,336 --> 00:34:39,629
Are you okay?

428
00:34:40,171 --> 00:34:41,380
She should be fine now.

429
00:34:42,298 --> 00:34:43,341
I'm not sure
what was choking her, though.

430
00:34:45,885 --> 00:34:46,969
- What...
- What's that?

431
00:34:47,053 --> 00:34:48,137
What is this?

432
00:35:09,200 --> 00:35:10,326
Oh, what's up?

433
00:35:10,660 --> 00:35:12,495
Listen up, everyone.
I've got big news.

434
00:35:12,578 --> 00:35:13,746
Did you guys hear?

435
00:35:13,829 --> 00:35:17,208
A new recruit named Nam Da-reum
made big trouble from day one.

436
00:35:18,125 --> 00:35:20,294
I mean, where is the discipline
in new recruits these days?

437
00:35:22,672 --> 00:35:23,714
What?

438
00:35:29,178 --> 00:35:30,638
Mr. Lee Jin-sang.

439
00:35:34,684 --> 00:35:35,768
Oops.

440
00:35:36,435 --> 00:35:37,436
My mistake.

441
00:35:40,565 --> 00:35:41,566
Go on.

442
00:35:45,903 --> 00:35:48,823
I threw up on Director Lee's pants
at my first company dinner.

443
00:35:51,826 --> 00:35:54,078
Anyone can make a mistake
when they're nervous.

444
00:35:54,579 --> 00:35:55,830
Don't worry about it.

445
00:35:57,999 --> 00:36:00,751
Thank you, Ms. Kim.

446
00:36:03,754 --> 00:36:06,048
Excuse me.

447
00:36:06,632 --> 00:36:10,386
But wasn't Mr. Lee Chan the CEO?

448
00:36:10,886 --> 00:36:13,389
The two were previously co-CEOs

449
00:36:13,472 --> 00:36:15,850
but recently, the system changed
and we now have one CEO.

450
00:36:16,726 --> 00:36:19,770
- Then...
- Director Lee is only in charge

451
00:36:19,854 --> 00:36:21,522
of the fashion
for Appello's key events.

452
00:36:25,234 --> 00:36:26,527
I see.

453
00:36:38,414 --> 00:36:39,999
What was it like
to finally see him in person?

454
00:36:40,082 --> 00:36:41,250
Did you manage to stay composed?

455
00:36:41,959 --> 00:36:45,338
A tear emoji? You must've cried.
Were you that moved?

456
00:36:45,421 --> 00:36:47,423
Let's throw a party
to remember your "made-it" moment.

457
00:36:47,506 --> 00:36:49,133
- What do you want to eat?
- I'm in!

458
00:36:49,216 --> 00:36:51,093
Let's eat
whatever Namda wants to eat today.

459
00:36:51,177 --> 00:36:52,511
- I'm in!
- I'm in!

460
00:36:52,595 --> 00:36:54,055
- We're in!
- We're in!

461
00:36:55,473 --> 00:36:58,601
<i>Girls, this is Chan's company</i>

462
00:36:59,018 --> 00:37:00,728
<i>but he's not around.</i>

463
00:37:02,021 --> 00:37:04,023
That's like saying
there are no pads in push-up bras.

464
00:37:04,106 --> 00:37:05,775
That one has 4cm pads.

465
00:37:06,525 --> 00:37:08,152
- It's thick.
- Right. Sure.

466
00:37:08,235 --> 00:37:10,321
I'll take this in all colors.

467
00:37:10,655 --> 00:37:11,781
<i>On top of that</i>

468
00:37:12,907 --> 00:37:15,618
<i>I ended up in our CEO's arms
on my first day.</i>

469
00:37:15,701 --> 00:37:16,744
What?

470
00:37:18,954 --> 00:37:20,414
What kind
of crazy development is this?

471
00:37:22,583 --> 00:37:25,044
<i>I'm done for!</i>

472
00:37:35,179 --> 00:37:39,100
So the one
who slammed her face into your chest

473
00:37:39,183 --> 00:37:40,267
was Ms. Nam Da-reum?

474
00:37:41,602 --> 00:37:45,231
She's from SE Corporation
of all places.

475
00:37:45,523 --> 00:37:46,816
Something doesn't feel right.

476
00:37:47,316 --> 00:37:49,485
If she had put it on her resume,
I wouldn't have hired her.

477
00:37:49,568 --> 00:37:50,861
COMPUTER SKILLS LEVEL 1,
SURVEY ANALYST LEVEL 2...

478
00:37:51,362 --> 00:37:53,739
I don't see a reason
why she wants to work at Appello.

479
00:37:56,784 --> 00:37:58,536
Mr. Kang, do you think

480
00:37:58,744 --> 00:38:00,955
she could be a corporate spy
working with Director Kim?

481
00:38:02,206 --> 00:38:04,041
I looked into it and found out that

482
00:38:04,125 --> 00:38:07,378
he has infiltrated a few businesses
with spies to take them over.

483
00:38:10,297 --> 00:38:12,758
Let's keep
a close eye on her for a while.

484
00:38:27,356 --> 00:38:29,191
In a way, Appello is quite smart.

485
00:38:29,567 --> 00:38:31,944
Everyone is busy
trying to snatch famous designers

486
00:38:32,027 --> 00:38:33,571
but you're going after new ones.

487
00:38:34,780 --> 00:38:36,031
It was Director Lee's idea.

488
00:38:36,490 --> 00:38:37,992
He was sad to see
talented brands disappear

489
00:38:38,075 --> 00:38:40,828
due to their lack of network
in distribution.

490
00:38:40,911 --> 00:38:42,997
Have you two always known each other?

491
00:38:43,289 --> 00:38:44,457
We went to high school together.

492
00:38:44,665 --> 00:38:46,375
Oh, you two must be best friends.

493
00:38:47,293 --> 00:38:48,794
That's why
he left the business with you.

494
00:38:57,762 --> 00:38:59,972
Goodness. I look forward
to working with you.

495
00:39:00,055 --> 00:39:02,808
SE Corporation is now taking part
in the e-commerce industry.

496
00:39:03,058 --> 00:39:05,394
We plan to open up
a fashion platform very soon.

497
00:39:05,686 --> 00:39:08,731
Wait, does that mean
you're competing against Appello?

498
00:39:09,398 --> 00:39:11,108
Compete? Hardly.

499
00:39:11,609 --> 00:39:13,402
We need to be similar in size
for that to happen.

500
00:39:14,528 --> 00:39:17,031
Wouldn't it be weirder
if we fail to lead the market

501
00:39:17,114 --> 00:39:19,617
with our resources
and distribution network?

502
00:39:24,622 --> 00:39:27,958
So you used investment as an excuse
to get our intel, in case you fail.

503
00:39:28,667 --> 00:39:31,629
I heard you've done that
with a few businesses with spies.

504
00:39:32,338 --> 00:39:33,547
Spies?

505
00:39:35,174 --> 00:39:36,842
Then what about Appello?

506
00:39:37,384 --> 00:39:40,304
Do you think one of my people
is there or not?

507
00:40:21,929 --> 00:40:23,514
CEO Kang Ha-gi?

508
00:40:25,015 --> 00:40:27,309
I am Reporter Do Eun-yong
with Insight Business Newspaper.

509
00:40:28,853 --> 00:40:30,604
INSIGHT BUSINESS NEWSPAPER
REPORTER DO EUN-YONG

510
00:40:31,105 --> 00:40:33,732
Nice to meet you. I look forward
to seeing great articles about us.

511
00:40:37,987 --> 00:40:41,198
Why don't you spare me some time?
I have many questions for you.

512
00:40:41,824 --> 00:40:43,826
Please contact my office
to schedule an interview.

513
00:40:43,909 --> 00:40:44,910
I don't mean Appello.

514
00:40:45,661 --> 00:40:46,704
I mean for you.

515
00:40:55,004 --> 00:40:56,881
<i>I'm almost there. See you soon.</i>

516
00:40:56,964 --> 00:40:58,424
I'm sorry. I must be somewhere.

517
00:41:00,384 --> 00:41:01,385
Are you done?

518
00:41:18,277 --> 00:41:19,904
Why are you so dressed up?

519
00:41:20,571 --> 00:41:22,114
You're wearing perfume too.

520
00:41:22,448 --> 00:41:23,908
Stop getting clingy.

521
00:41:23,991 --> 00:41:26,660
Why? It's been so long
since we've met.

522
00:41:29,246 --> 00:41:30,539
You only call me for business.

523
00:41:31,373 --> 00:41:33,584
Why are you staying at a hotel
and not at your place?

524
00:41:34,209 --> 00:41:35,336
Someone kept visiting me.

525
00:41:37,338 --> 00:41:39,673
Be careful.
That can turn into an owner's risk.

526
00:41:40,049 --> 00:41:41,508
We're over already

527
00:41:41,717 --> 00:41:42,760
and it was an industry insider.

528
00:41:43,552 --> 00:41:45,054
You'd better keep that up.

529
00:41:46,889 --> 00:41:49,058
Only date someone
who has something to lose.

530
00:41:52,061 --> 00:41:55,147
I knew it.
That's the CEO Kang Ha-gi I know.

531
00:41:56,148 --> 00:41:57,942
This is why
you haven't dated in a decade...

532
00:41:58,817 --> 00:42:01,362
Never mind. You were unable to date.

533
00:42:01,445 --> 00:42:02,488
You're so cold-hearted.

534
00:42:02,947 --> 00:42:04,823
Find a hobby.

535
00:42:04,907 --> 00:42:06,283
Or start stanning a star.

536
00:42:07,660 --> 00:42:08,661
I already have a bias.

537
00:42:11,747 --> 00:42:13,666
You? Who?

538
00:42:15,417 --> 00:42:16,543
Appello.

539
00:42:17,628 --> 00:42:18,629
I already know.

540
00:42:19,046 --> 00:42:21,131
You like me. Say it's me.

541
00:42:21,548 --> 00:42:22,925
Just say it's me.

542
00:42:23,008 --> 00:42:25,636
Say, "Lee Chan."
Say, "Lee Chan is my bias."

543
00:42:25,719 --> 00:42:27,805
- Appello.
- Lee Chan.

544
00:42:28,222 --> 00:42:29,848
- Appello.
- Lee Chan.

545
00:42:29,932 --> 00:42:31,266
- Appello.
- I'll bite you.

546
00:42:31,350 --> 00:42:32,810
I knew it.

547
00:42:54,999 --> 00:42:56,166
What's with her now?

548
00:42:56,250 --> 00:42:57,334
Let her be.

549
00:42:57,418 --> 00:43:00,170
Hey, Namda!
Come and eat some fried chicken!

550
00:43:00,587 --> 00:43:01,588
No!

551
00:43:02,047 --> 00:43:04,091
I still have a long way to go!

552
00:43:11,557 --> 00:43:12,641
Hey, Mi-mi.

553
00:43:12,933 --> 00:43:16,228
Can I just do
a hundred of these again?

554
00:43:16,311 --> 00:43:19,314
I need to drain myself to forget
what happened at the CEO's office...

555
00:43:23,235 --> 00:43:24,361
It's coming back.

556
00:43:24,445 --> 00:43:27,072
You don't have to mind it.
Things like that happen in life.

557
00:43:27,614 --> 00:43:28,699
It can't.

558
00:43:30,284 --> 00:43:34,038
Guys, how am I going
to face the CEO from now on?

559
00:43:34,455 --> 00:43:36,832
And what about the entire company
thinking I'm a weird woman?

560
00:43:41,253 --> 00:43:42,546
It was only your first day.

561
00:43:42,629 --> 00:43:44,381
If you do your job well

562
00:43:44,465 --> 00:43:45,799
these rumors will die down quickly.

563
00:43:47,926 --> 00:43:49,803
- Do you think so?
- Of course.

564
00:43:50,262 --> 00:43:52,264
And you're just a rookie.

565
00:43:52,347 --> 00:43:53,682
You won't have to meet the CEO often.

566
00:43:54,016 --> 00:43:55,142
Just avoid him.

567
00:43:56,477 --> 00:43:57,519
Right?

568
00:43:58,979 --> 00:44:02,608
I won't have to meet the CEO

569
00:44:03,275 --> 00:44:04,443
at all, right?

570
00:44:05,110 --> 00:44:06,820
- Not at all.
- Not likely.

571
00:44:08,113 --> 00:44:11,366
Right.
Yes, I doubt I'll have to see him.

572
00:44:11,450 --> 00:44:13,035
No, never again.

573
00:44:16,455 --> 00:44:18,624
I'll work hard
and improve my reputation.

574
00:44:18,999 --> 00:44:20,000
As for the CEO...

575
00:44:21,043 --> 00:44:22,211
I'll avoid him.

576
00:44:22,669 --> 00:44:23,712
Yes.

577
00:44:33,555 --> 00:44:35,849
It's our first pop-up store
since TUNZI's launch

578
00:44:35,933 --> 00:44:37,893
so please pay extra attention.

579
00:44:37,976 --> 00:44:38,977
- Yes.
- Yes, ma'am.

580
00:44:46,735 --> 00:44:50,030
TUNZI IS A SPACE
FOR DESIGNER MIN-JI'S...

581
00:44:59,915 --> 00:45:00,958
I'll do it!

582
00:45:11,510 --> 00:45:12,761
Let me help!

583
00:45:20,018 --> 00:45:21,854
I'll take it!

584
00:45:36,577 --> 00:45:37,619
TUNZI OUTFIT SETTING LIST

585
00:46:02,561 --> 00:46:03,937
<i>The doors are closing.</i>

586
00:46:07,816 --> 00:46:09,026
Work hard.

587
00:46:09,109 --> 00:46:11,570
Avoid the CEO.

588
00:46:27,169 --> 00:46:28,337
<i>The doors are closing.</i>

589
00:46:31,757 --> 00:46:35,177
Hello, we're the rookie employees,
Nam Da-reum...

590
00:46:35,260 --> 00:46:37,095
- Park Young-woo...
- And Lee Min-a!

591
00:46:37,179 --> 00:46:38,513
- Nice to meet you.
- Nice to meet you.

592
00:46:40,224 --> 00:46:41,266
- Hello.
- How cute.

593
00:46:41,350 --> 00:46:43,185
- I love the energy.
- It's great to meet you.

594
00:46:43,268 --> 00:46:44,686
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

595
00:46:45,604 --> 00:46:47,356
- We'll do our best!
- We'll do our best!

596
00:46:48,357 --> 00:46:50,567
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

597
00:46:50,651 --> 00:46:51,860
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

598
00:46:51,944 --> 00:46:53,278
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

599
00:46:53,362 --> 00:46:56,031
- We'll do our best!
- We'll do our best!

600
00:46:57,574 --> 00:46:58,700
Thank you.

601
00:46:59,534 --> 00:47:01,203
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

602
00:47:25,727 --> 00:47:28,981
Here comes CEO Kang Ha-gi!

603
00:47:35,946 --> 00:47:36,989
Hello, Mr. Kang!

604
00:47:37,197 --> 00:47:39,283
- Hello, Mr. Kang!
- Hello, Mr. Kang!

605
00:47:39,491 --> 00:47:41,868
- Hello.
- Mr. Kang, please sit over here.

606
00:47:41,952 --> 00:47:44,579
Goodness, no. Why this table?

607
00:47:48,292 --> 00:47:49,334
Have a seat.

608
00:47:52,713 --> 00:47:54,381
I thought you'd be too busy to come.

609
00:47:54,464 --> 00:47:55,799
I have to leave soon

610
00:47:55,882 --> 00:47:57,384
for a video meeting
with a foreign VC firm.

611
00:47:57,467 --> 00:47:58,844
Mr. Kang, would you like a drink

612
00:47:58,927 --> 00:48:00,846
- I have a video meeting.
- Yes, right.

613
00:48:00,929 --> 00:48:02,764
- Can you pour me one?
- Have some.

614
00:48:04,975 --> 00:48:06,518
Why did the atmosphere turn gloomy?

615
00:48:06,601 --> 00:48:09,855
Everyone! Drink up. Come on.

616
00:48:09,938 --> 00:48:12,190
CEO Ha-gi is with us now

617
00:48:12,274 --> 00:48:15,110
so let's have a drink happily!
Drink up!

618
00:48:15,193 --> 00:48:16,737
- Drink up!
- Mr. Kang.

619
00:48:17,029 --> 00:48:18,363
Right. You aren't drinking.

620
00:48:18,822 --> 00:48:20,324
Please give us your guidance.

621
00:48:20,407 --> 00:48:21,992
We look forward to learning a lot.

622
00:48:26,371 --> 00:48:27,914
Let's call it a day quickly.

623
00:48:28,457 --> 00:48:29,875
Don't let the rookies get too drunk.

624
00:48:30,167 --> 00:48:31,209
Yes, sir.

625
00:48:34,838 --> 00:48:36,048
Let's keep drinking!

626
00:48:36,465 --> 00:48:38,925
Da-reum is at a company dinner,
and I'm really concerned.

627
00:48:39,718 --> 00:48:41,887
She'll chug every single drink
without turning anything down.

628
00:48:41,970 --> 00:48:43,472
She's a born nerd.

629
00:48:44,139 --> 00:48:45,766
That's the problem with Namda.

630
00:48:46,516 --> 00:48:48,810
She tries too hard.

631
00:49:02,366 --> 00:49:03,950
- Oh, wow.
- Manager, please have one.

632
00:49:04,034 --> 00:49:05,952
What? Me?

633
00:49:07,371 --> 00:49:09,623
Gosh, Da-reum. I didn't know
you were capable of this.

634
00:49:09,706 --> 00:49:11,375
I learned it from my friends.

635
00:49:11,458 --> 00:49:14,169
You have great friends.
Wait a second, sweetie.

636
00:49:15,796 --> 00:49:16,963
You need a drink from me.

637
00:49:17,297 --> 00:49:18,340
Of course.

638
00:49:18,799 --> 00:49:20,675
- All right.
- Ms. Nam Da-reum.

639
00:49:21,259 --> 00:49:22,344
Sorry?

640
00:49:23,136 --> 00:49:24,137
Take a drink from me instead.

641
00:49:25,806 --> 00:49:27,766
Right. Yes!

642
00:49:29,226 --> 00:49:30,560
Yes, right. Yes.

643
00:49:31,978 --> 00:49:33,105
Use that glass.

644
00:49:33,688 --> 00:49:35,357
Right. Yes, sir!

645
00:49:36,233 --> 00:49:37,234
Okay.

646
00:49:38,568 --> 00:49:39,569
What?

647
00:49:43,281 --> 00:49:44,282
Team dinners are voluntary.

648
00:49:45,575 --> 00:49:46,868
If you're exhausted, you may go home.

649
00:49:49,579 --> 00:49:51,498
Yes, sir. I will.

650
00:50:18,900 --> 00:50:20,902
MEAT BARBECUE

651
00:50:22,779 --> 00:50:27,200
I should go for a quick recharge.

652
00:50:30,495 --> 00:50:32,372
- Drink up!
- Cheers!

653
00:50:33,790 --> 00:50:35,876
- Cheers!
- Have another drink.

654
00:50:36,293 --> 00:50:38,253
I have to be at a meeting soon,
so please excuse me.

655
00:50:38,545 --> 00:50:40,464
Yes, you should get going, Mr. Kang.

656
00:50:41,339 --> 00:50:43,049
Goodbye, Mr. Kang.

657
00:50:46,553 --> 00:50:47,637
Oh, okay.

658
00:50:49,681 --> 00:50:52,017
- I need some more.
- Come on!

659
00:51:04,362 --> 00:51:05,655
Why is Director Kim here?

660
00:51:19,252 --> 00:51:20,921
Darn it.

661
00:51:55,611 --> 00:51:58,948
If I work hard enough

662
00:51:59,449 --> 00:52:00,616
then one day

663
00:52:03,202 --> 00:52:06,664
I'll get to see you in person, right?

664
00:52:13,045 --> 00:52:16,591
Anyway, he looks really good
in this picture.

665
00:52:18,468 --> 00:52:21,304
I must take a picture.

666
00:52:27,477 --> 00:52:28,728
PASSCODE

667
00:52:29,687 --> 00:52:31,147
Why isn't it working?

668
00:52:32,148 --> 00:52:35,151
Zero. Nine. One. Six.

669
00:52:38,154 --> 00:52:40,781
That's Chan's birthday.

670
00:52:41,449 --> 00:52:45,745
Zero. Nine. One...

671
00:52:56,923 --> 00:52:57,924
Ms. Nam.

672
00:52:58,716 --> 00:52:59,759
Yes?

673
00:53:00,968 --> 00:53:02,512
What do you think you're doing here?

674
00:53:04,388 --> 00:53:05,515
Mr. Kang?

675
00:53:05,598 --> 00:53:07,183
Why are you here
in the middle of a company dinner?

676
00:53:07,600 --> 00:53:08,601
What?

677
00:53:09,060 --> 00:53:10,520
Me? You mean me?

678
00:53:11,062 --> 00:53:13,231
Oh, I...

679
00:53:13,439 --> 00:53:16,275
I needed to recharge for a bit.

680
00:53:16,943 --> 00:53:19,862
- Recharge?
- You said you always

681
00:53:20,905 --> 00:53:22,615
welcomed everyone

682
00:53:22,698 --> 00:53:24,200
and that your office

683
00:53:25,117 --> 00:53:27,495
was always open.

684
00:53:28,454 --> 00:53:31,249
So a picture.

685
00:53:31,874 --> 00:53:36,754
I was going to leave
after taking just one picture.

686
00:53:38,548 --> 00:53:39,549
What picture?

687
00:53:40,299 --> 00:53:41,300
A picture...

688
00:53:55,147 --> 00:53:57,984
Now, everyone. Attention, please.

689
00:53:58,776 --> 00:54:02,238
There is one question all rookies
of our company must answer.

690
00:54:02,321 --> 00:54:03,406
Yes, that one.

691
00:54:03,489 --> 00:54:05,992
Now, dear adorable Ms. Lee Min-a

692
00:54:06,075 --> 00:54:09,829
are you on Team Ha-gi or Team Chan?

693
00:54:10,913 --> 00:54:12,957
- What?
- Do you prefer someone like Mr. Kang

694
00:54:13,040 --> 00:54:14,667
who's very trustworthy

695
00:54:14,750 --> 00:54:16,586
and hard on the outside,
but soft on the inside?

696
00:54:16,669 --> 00:54:18,170
Or is it Director Chan

697
00:54:18,254 --> 00:54:20,339
someone unreal,
like he popped out of a fairy tale?

698
00:54:21,465 --> 00:54:23,509
Well, the thing is

699
00:54:23,593 --> 00:54:25,761
there's too much pressure.

700
00:54:25,845 --> 00:54:29,223
If they're too much pressure for you,
you can join Team Jin-sang.

701
00:54:29,849 --> 00:54:31,392
- Join me.
- What?

702
00:54:32,310 --> 00:54:34,186
- What?
- Come on. You ruined it.

703
00:54:34,270 --> 00:54:35,563
Hurry up and choose.

704
00:54:35,646 --> 00:54:37,565
In that case, I choose...

705
00:54:43,738 --> 00:54:46,032
Team Ha-gi.

706
00:54:47,408 --> 00:54:48,951
- I knew it.
- I was right.

707
00:54:49,035 --> 00:54:50,286
See? Me too.

708
00:54:50,369 --> 00:54:51,996
- Nice choice, Min-a.
- I was right.

709
00:54:52,079 --> 00:54:53,331
- I had a feeling.
- I'm on Team Ha-gi too!

710
00:54:53,414 --> 00:54:55,249
Why is everyone on Team Ha-gi?

711
00:54:55,333 --> 00:54:57,501
- Is anybody on Team Jin-sang?
- It's Ha-gi.

712
00:55:22,485 --> 00:55:25,071
Did she really break in
because she was just drunk?

713
00:55:34,372 --> 00:55:35,956
{\an8}<i>Well, Mr. Kang.</i>

714
00:55:36,165 --> 00:55:39,463
{\an8}<i>I have to stay that was a
very impressive presentation.</i>

715
00:55:39,543 --> 00:55:41,420
{\an8}<i>Your platform's growth metrics</i>

716
00:55:42,046 --> 00:55:43,547
{\an8}<i>are outstanding.</i>

717
00:55:43,964 --> 00:55:46,175
{\an8}<i>And the "Unframe" philosophy?</i>

718
00:55:47,635 --> 00:55:49,637
{\an8}<i>What a brilliant differentiator</i>

719
00:55:49,804 --> 00:55:52,264
{\an8}<i>in what is a very crowded market.</i>

720
00:55:52,556 --> 00:55:54,228
{\an8}<i>Our team will be in touch with you
within the week</i>

721
00:55:54,308 --> 00:55:55,726
{\an8}<i>to discuss the next steps.</i>

722
00:55:56,227 --> 00:55:58,024
{\an8}<i>It's a pleasure speaking with you,
Mr. Kang.</i>

723
00:55:58,104 --> 00:56:00,606
{\an8}Thank you. I hope to see you soon.

724
00:56:00,815 --> 00:56:02,358
{\an8}<i>You bet. Take care.</i>

725
00:56:39,895 --> 00:56:41,188
She didn't hear that, did she?

726
00:56:47,611 --> 00:56:48,612
Ms. Nam.

727
00:57:02,376 --> 00:57:03,919
Ms. Nam, time to go home.

728
00:57:04,587 --> 00:57:06,130
Wake up, Ms. Nam.

729
00:57:07,882 --> 00:57:10,050
What? Why?

730
00:57:22,563 --> 00:57:24,482
She's driving me insane.

731
00:57:26,734 --> 00:57:27,943
What now?

732
00:58:04,563 --> 00:58:05,731
I must be insane.

733
00:58:08,067 --> 00:58:09,401
I must be.

734
00:58:11,153 --> 00:58:12,488
Yes, I am.

735
00:58:16,242 --> 00:58:17,660
Oh, come on.

736
00:58:23,082 --> 00:58:24,542
I feel like throwing up.

737
00:58:34,844 --> 00:58:37,304
What? You did it with the CEO...

738
00:58:41,517 --> 00:58:45,479
- You slept with him?
- What? No!

739
00:58:45,563 --> 00:58:48,941
I fell asleep in his office.

740
00:58:52,611 --> 00:58:54,822
I knew it. There's no way
our conservative girl would do that.

741
00:58:55,614 --> 00:58:57,074
So why did you go there?

742
00:58:59,410 --> 00:59:00,536
No idea.

743
00:59:01,036 --> 00:59:02,538
I guess
I was in my zombie mode again.

744
00:59:03,330 --> 00:59:05,249
There's a picture of Chan there.

745
00:59:05,332 --> 00:59:08,669
It's not a photoshoot, though.
It's such a candid picture.

746
00:59:08,752 --> 00:59:09,920
You're insane.

747
00:59:11,463 --> 00:59:13,465
You have to do something
about your drunken behavior.

748
00:59:13,549 --> 00:59:15,885
Da-reum,
you literally are killing me.

749
00:59:16,635 --> 00:59:19,889
I'm sorry.
I'll seriously quit drinking now.

750
00:59:20,222 --> 00:59:21,223
Jeez!

751
00:59:24,810 --> 00:59:27,313
Anyway, you didn't do
anything weird in the office, right?

752
00:59:27,813 --> 00:59:28,814
I

753
00:59:29,565 --> 00:59:30,816
hope not.

754
00:59:33,152 --> 00:59:34,945
What is this ominous feeling?

755
00:59:35,029 --> 00:59:37,031
- I don't know.
- Wait, no.

756
00:59:38,574 --> 00:59:39,700
Did you black out?

757
00:59:40,784 --> 00:59:41,827
Yes.

758
00:59:46,206 --> 00:59:47,541
Hey, Da-reum.

759
00:59:47,625 --> 00:59:50,127
- Hello.
- Oh, hello.

760
01:00:03,599 --> 01:00:05,809
Hey, Nam Da-reum!

761
01:00:06,810 --> 01:00:08,437
I saw a new side of you yesterday.

762
01:00:08,520 --> 01:00:10,648
You did something with this thing

763
01:00:10,731 --> 01:00:14,902
and bang, the bottle cap spun around,
flew over there, and blast!

764
01:00:16,570 --> 01:00:18,030
Gosh, you truly are different.

765
01:00:18,781 --> 01:00:20,199
- Give me five.
- What?

766
01:00:21,241 --> 01:00:24,119
M-Me? What did I do? Why...

767
01:00:26,914 --> 01:00:27,915
What's going on?

768
01:00:29,083 --> 01:00:30,876
You were so cool yesterday, Da-reum.

769
01:00:30,960 --> 01:00:32,127
You're the best, Da-reum.

770
01:00:43,806 --> 01:00:46,225
- Good morning.
- Good morning.

771
01:00:51,647 --> 01:00:52,773
- Da-reum.
- Yes?

772
01:00:52,856 --> 01:00:54,233
Did you get home safely last night?

773
01:00:54,441 --> 01:00:55,985
You seemed to have left
after getting drunk.

774
01:00:56,235 --> 01:00:57,778
Yes, I did.

775
01:01:05,953 --> 01:01:08,539
He's so good-looking.

776
01:01:08,622 --> 01:01:11,041
Ms. Nam.

777
01:01:12,418 --> 01:01:14,545
<i>Wait, what is this memory?</i>

778
01:01:15,087 --> 01:01:16,755
<i>It feels like Mr. Kang was there.</i>

779
01:01:17,965 --> 01:01:20,092
- Excuse me, Ms. Kim.
- Yes?

780
01:01:20,175 --> 01:01:23,429
By any chance, is Mr. Kang at work?

781
01:01:23,512 --> 01:01:24,596
Mr. Kang?

782
01:01:24,847 --> 01:01:26,640
I think
he spent the night up in his office.

783
01:01:27,016 --> 01:01:28,017
What?

784
01:01:35,816 --> 01:01:37,526
<i>Darn it. What's going on?</i>

785
01:01:37,735 --> 01:01:39,820
<i>What happened?
Why is he looking at me?</i>

786
01:01:40,154 --> 01:01:43,657
<i>Please recall it.
Think hard, Nam Da-reum.</i>

787
01:01:44,033 --> 01:01:46,118
SAMPLE ROOM

788
01:01:58,213 --> 01:02:00,215
I don't think I've sobered up yet.

789
01:02:00,674 --> 01:02:03,135
Da-reum! You were here?

790
01:02:03,469 --> 01:02:05,220
- Do you feel okay?
- Yes.

791
01:02:06,472 --> 01:02:08,348
I got wasted last night, wasn't I?

792
01:02:08,640 --> 01:02:10,726
Did I make any mistakes?

793
01:02:10,809 --> 01:02:13,062
Mistakes? What mistakes?

794
01:02:13,145 --> 01:02:14,855
You left early,
so you didn't have time to do that.

795
01:02:14,938 --> 01:02:19,318
Da-reum, it would've been so much fun
if you stayed until the very end.

796
01:02:19,401 --> 01:02:22,237
At the end of the night,
Director Lee Chan came!

797
01:02:22,321 --> 01:02:23,947
He was so good-looking.

798
01:02:24,907 --> 01:02:25,949
What?

799
01:02:26,825 --> 01:02:27,951
My goodness.

800
01:02:28,035 --> 01:02:31,371
I thought he was just good-looking,
but he was hilarious too.

801
01:02:31,455 --> 01:02:32,664
- Yes.
- See?

802
01:02:32,748 --> 01:02:35,417
He only took a picture with us
to congratulate us on our start here!

803
01:02:40,172 --> 01:02:41,590
My Chan was there?

804
01:02:43,509 --> 01:02:47,846
You should call him
Director Lee at work.

805
01:02:47,930 --> 01:02:50,891
Shouldn't we call him that?

806
01:02:51,725 --> 01:02:55,020
Wait, Da-reum must've been
a fan of D.N.X.

807
01:02:55,312 --> 01:02:56,939
I almost said, "It's Lee Chan!"

808
01:02:57,648 --> 01:02:58,690
It could've been a mistake.

809
01:02:59,108 --> 01:03:00,109
Oh, no.

810
01:03:01,026 --> 01:03:02,528
What's wrong, Da-reum?

811
01:03:03,320 --> 01:03:04,863
Was it something I said?

812
01:03:08,325 --> 01:03:09,493
It's not that.

813
01:03:10,994 --> 01:03:12,121
It's nothing.

814
01:03:23,173 --> 01:03:24,550
Not only was I drunk

815
01:03:25,926 --> 01:03:28,095
but I broke into the CEO's office

816
01:03:30,639 --> 01:03:32,224
and didn't even get to see my Chan.

817
01:03:38,188 --> 01:03:40,107
Why are you even alive, Da-reum?

818
01:03:41,483 --> 01:03:43,318
Just end yourself.

819
01:03:45,654 --> 01:03:48,574
That was my chance
to finally see him in person.

820
01:04:33,118 --> 01:04:34,119
Oh, mother!

821
01:04:37,497 --> 01:04:39,917
Why do you always look for your mom
whenever you see me?

822
01:04:41,335 --> 01:04:43,086
So, about yesterday...

823
01:04:45,839 --> 01:04:47,090
I'm sorry, Mr. Kang.

824
01:04:47,758 --> 01:04:50,802
I remember getting drunk
and walking into your office.

825
01:04:51,345 --> 01:04:53,388
But when I opened my eyes,
it was already morning.

826
01:04:56,767 --> 01:04:57,851
So you don't remember?

827
01:04:59,436 --> 01:05:01,688
How convenient.
You never remember anything.

828
01:05:03,023 --> 01:05:04,566
- Sorry?
- Forget it.

829
01:05:05,317 --> 01:05:06,443
It's better that way.

830
01:05:07,653 --> 01:05:08,987
I wanted to wake you
when you sobered up.

831
01:05:09,071 --> 01:05:11,073
But you were too drunk to do that.

832
01:05:11,365 --> 01:05:14,117
Then what about you?

833
01:05:17,287 --> 01:05:18,288
Well...

834
01:05:21,333 --> 01:05:22,334
I worked and left.

835
01:05:24,962 --> 01:05:27,089
Yes, right? I'm glad.

836
01:05:27,547 --> 01:05:28,924
I'm glad you didn't stay
because of me.

837
01:05:29,007 --> 01:05:30,133
Please be cautious from now on.

838
01:05:30,217 --> 01:05:31,260
That kind of behavior

839
01:05:32,094 --> 01:05:33,720
may cause
an unnecessary misunderstanding.

840
01:05:35,430 --> 01:05:36,431
Yes, sir.

841
01:05:36,848 --> 01:05:38,058
I'm sorry, Mr. Kang.

842
01:05:38,392 --> 01:05:40,102
I won't let
anything like this happen again.

843
01:05:42,145 --> 01:05:43,146
I'm sorry.

844
01:05:47,567 --> 01:05:49,111
- Yes, Ms. Kim.
<i>- Hey, Da-reum.</i>

845
01:05:49,194 --> 01:05:51,947
<i>Go to the showroom on the first floor
and help out with organizing.</i>

846
01:05:52,030 --> 01:05:53,240
Yes, coming.

847
01:05:54,866 --> 01:05:57,035
Ms. Kim needs me at the showroom

848
01:05:57,119 --> 01:05:58,829
so please excuse me.

849
01:06:08,630 --> 01:06:09,756
Ms. Nam.

850
01:06:14,344 --> 01:06:15,595
What? Why is he following me?

851
01:06:28,734 --> 01:06:31,111
<i>The miracle I had always hoped for</i>

852
01:06:32,988 --> 01:06:34,823
<i>did not happen on a special day.</i>

853
01:06:36,908 --> 01:06:39,786
<i>It came into my trivial daily life</i>

854
01:06:42,456 --> 01:06:45,417
<i>in the least expected moment.</i>

855
01:07:19,951 --> 01:07:23,538
{\an8}MY BIAS, MY BOSS

856
01:07:34,591 --> 01:07:35,926
{\an8}CHEON SEON-AE

857
01:07:36,009 --> 01:07:37,552
{\an8}EPILOGUE

858
01:08:22,013 --> 01:08:24,516
<i>Scrub with love</i>

859
01:08:24,599 --> 01:08:28,019
<i>Scrub the dirt off your heart</i>

860
01:08:28,562 --> 01:08:31,940
<i>Every corner, every grime</i>

861
01:08:32,023 --> 01:08:34,568
<i>Let me scrub it off for you</i>

862
01:08:35,569 --> 01:08:39,448
<i>Scrub, scrub with love</i>

863
01:08:39,531 --> 01:08:42,868
<i>The dirt on the bruise of your heart</i>

864
01:08:43,118 --> 01:08:46,163
<i>I will even scrub the bruises</i>

865
01:08:46,538 --> 01:08:51,918
<i>Of your heart with my love</i>

866
01:08:52,002 --> 01:08:53,378
<i>Scrub, scrub</i>

867
01:08:53,795 --> 01:08:55,380
- Oh, my. Mr. Kang.
- Goodness.

868
01:08:56,339 --> 01:08:59,092
I mean,
it's a good morning, Ms. Cheon.

869
01:08:59,176 --> 01:09:01,178
Oh, no.
Did you spend the night up again?

870
01:09:01,261 --> 01:09:02,596
You should take a quick nap.

871
01:09:02,679 --> 01:09:04,306
I'll clean up quickly and leave.

872
01:09:09,269 --> 01:09:11,730
No, it's all right.

873
01:09:11,813 --> 01:09:13,148
My paperwork is all over the place.

874
01:09:13,231 --> 01:09:15,525
That's nothing new.

875
01:09:15,609 --> 01:09:17,444
It's not like
I've ever touched anything.

876
01:09:17,527 --> 01:09:19,404
If you have work to do, go ahead.

877
01:09:19,488 --> 01:09:20,947
I'll make it quick and leave.

878
01:09:23,742 --> 01:09:25,577
Ms. Cheon.

879
01:09:26,953 --> 01:09:28,705
Dear Ms. Cheon.

880
01:09:30,332 --> 01:09:31,333
Would you like

881
01:09:32,292 --> 01:09:33,585
to have a cup of coffee with me?

882
01:09:34,461 --> 01:09:37,631
Coffee? Morning coffee sounds great.

883
01:09:38,548 --> 01:09:42,052
<i>Scrub, scrub, scrub the dirt</i>

884
01:09:49,100 --> 01:09:51,186
{\an8}- Nice to meet you, Da-reum.
- How do you know my name?

885
01:09:51,436 --> 01:09:52,771
{\an8}I'm not dreaming, am I?

886
01:09:53,605 --> 01:09:55,273
{\an8}<i>Overseas training
for outstanding employees?</i>

887
01:09:56,149 --> 01:09:58,401
{\an8}<i>I feel like she has a hidden agenda.</i>

888
01:09:58,485 --> 01:10:00,487
{\an8}Mr. Kang.

889
01:10:00,570 --> 01:10:02,447
{\an8}You look so cool today.

890
01:10:02,822 --> 01:10:04,866
{\an8}Maybe she's a honey trap

891
01:10:05,575 --> 01:10:06,701
{\an8}<i>Director Kim sent.</i>

892
01:10:06,952 --> 01:10:09,204
{\an8}<i>- Call me.</i>
- See you again!

893
01:10:10,705 --> 01:10:11,790
{\an8}<i>They're dating?</i>

894
01:10:11,873 --> 01:10:13,708
{\an8}<i>Our company CEO and Chan?</i>

895
01:10:13,792 --> 01:10:16,836
{\an8}<i>No!</i>

896
01:10:22,432 --> 01:10:27,657
{\an8}Synced and corrected by
WEISSACHsubs

